WEBVTT

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:05.210
No one's coming.

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.550
They're just running a little late.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.130
<b>Three Weeks Earlier</b>

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.170
Okay, here I go.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:26.960
Our field cleanup operation is complete!

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.510
Yay!

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.510
We're finally done!

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:30.150
What a great feeling!

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.820
At last, we're not
the "weeding association" anymore!

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.240
Now we can practice using the entire field!

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.720
That's right. Let's start with
our new practice regimen right away.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:41.610
Yeah!

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.190
But first, I have a suggestion!

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:46.520
Go on.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.020
So... why don't we play a real game?

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.990
<b>Our First Game!</b>

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.330
A practice game, huh?

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.220
Yeah! Our usual practices are fun,

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:33.240
but actual games are
what baseball is all about!

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:34.430
A contest?

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.130
That sounds fun!

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:38.760
Um, who will we play against?

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:41.280
I'll find an opponent soon.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.230
You didn't do that before suggesting it?

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:48.980
Ideally, it would be a girls' 
baseball team, like ours.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:51.340
C-Can we handle that?

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:54.130
Frankly, there's no way we can win.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:56.440
You say that so calmly.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.960
There's nothing to worry about!

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.580
It's only for practice.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.500
No matter how good the other team is,

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.230
we should just think of it as having
them help us and enjoy the experience.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:17.190
Y-You're right. We've been practicing 
for two months now, after all.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:22.280
To be honest, I've been thinking 
I'd like to play in a real game, too.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.440
A-Actually, so have I.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.060
That settles it, then!

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.700
I'll get in touch with
other schools in the prefecture

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.890
to help you find a team to play.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.520
Thank you, ma'am!

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:36.980
There's something I'd like to say too,
and this seems like a good time.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:38.780
What is it?

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:39.440
What?

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:43.260
I'm going to announce what
positions everyone will play.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:47.720
I took each person's
preferences into consideration,

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:50.630
and consulted with Arihara-san
and Shinonome-san to work it all out.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:52.280
Now...

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:55.160
First base: Nozaki-san.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.090
Okay!

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:58.120
On second: Kawakita-san.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.550
O-Okay!

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:01.560
On third: Asada-senpai.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.350
You got it!

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:05.810
Shortstop: Arihara-san.

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:07.010
Yep!

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:09.160
Left field: Iwaki-senpai.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:09.970
Right!

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.050
Center field: Nakano-san.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:13.440
Got it!

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.560
Right field: Ukita-san.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:16.900
O-Okay!

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.850
The catcher will be myself, Suzuki.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:21.360
And finally, our pitcher...

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.310
will be Shinonome-san.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:27.060
It's not my usual position, but all right.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.370
We'll be practicing for the game
 in these positions.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:25.720
If anyone has any questions, just ask!

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:26.350
Me!

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:28.090
I have a question!

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:29.350
Go ahead.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:32.060
Will we be playing the game
in our tracksuits?

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:37.690
We forgot!

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:40.150
Satogahama Baseball

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:40.150
Ten...

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:42.230
Ten thousand yen?!

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:45.370
Yeah. A complete uniform is 10,000 yen.

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:47.890
That's a fair price.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.990
Okay, then, let's use our club funds!

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:52.810
We have no money left.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:53.200
Huh?!

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.870
We spent all our funds on practice balls.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:06:00.670
<b>Practice Balls</b>

00:05:53.200 --> 00:06:00.670
<b>Practice Balls</b>

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.750
Associations don't receive 
that much funding, anyway.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:01.230
Our funds!

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:04.850
I guess we'll all have to ask our parents
to pay for our uniforms.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:07.460
That means getting
an advance on my allowance...

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.920
By the way, what kind of design did you want?

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:15.720
If you have any ideas in mind,
we can do them for you, within reason.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:19.360
Th-These are uniforms for the baseball team?

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.480
Yeah. You're in the art club,
right, Amakusa-san?

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:26.210
We were hoping you could use
these to come up with a design...

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:29.680
High school girls running
around on the field... blue sky...

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.700
The parabola drawn by the ball...

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:34.970
I've got it!

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.100
Ta-da!

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:41.020
A s-skirt?

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:42.500
I think it's cute!

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:43.590
Yeah!

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.700
If you all like it, I guess it's fine, but...

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:48.850
We're still an association,

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:51.230
but we're looking the part more and more.

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:52.540
Yeah!

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:53.600
Girls!

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:56.620
I found a team you can play 
a practice game with...

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.300
You did?!

00:06:58.300 --> 00:06:59.520
Yes...

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:04.610
<b>Girls' Baseball Association!</b>

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:04.610
Remember to knock!

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:02.800
Seijo? From the next town over?

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.610
Are they famous?

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:08.580
The boys' team is very good.
They've been to nationals before.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:10.570
I didn't know they had a girls' team.

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:13.040
I can't believe a school like that would...

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.990
I followed Nakano-san's advice

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:19.140
and told them we had players who have
been to the Senior Little League nationals,

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:20.840
and they were happy to agree!

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.740
They suggested a date two weeks from now.

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:28.790
That's not much time.

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:33.300
I'll try to come up with a strategy 
that'll give us the best chance to compete.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.500
In the meantime,
let's get plenty of practice in.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:37.080
Yeah!

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:38.120
We'll all work hard!

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.020
Let's do this!

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:42.250
Should they be celebrating this much?

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:45.980
For where we are now,
I think it's about right.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:56.990
Get a sense for how the ball moves!

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:21.410
So when that happens, use a bunt to...

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.400
They're done!

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:38.870
<b>Two Weeks Later</b>

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:42.830
I'm Jinguji Sayaka, captain of
the Seijo High School girls' baseball team.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.790
Let's make today's practice game a good one.

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:50.270
I'm Arihara Tsubasa of the Satogahama
High School baseball association.

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:52.260
Thanks for playing us today!

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:55.220
Play ball!

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.140
Strike!

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:21.740
Strike two!

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:24.080
<i>Two inside pitches in a row.</i>

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.830
<i>The next one will go outside.</i>

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:29.000
Strike three!

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:31.460
Wow!

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:35.730
<i>Those pitches were good.</i>

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:38.350
<i>I'm not very good at catching curveballs yet,</i>

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:41.470
<i>but Shinonome-san's sharp fastballs
do the job just fine.</i>

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.460
<i>If she can vary its flight and speed...</i>

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:45.850
Strike three!

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.110
<i>They won't be easy to hit.</i>

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:49.800
Strike three!

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:53.440
Nice pitching!

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:54.740
Thanks.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:57.230
Let's go.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:58.200
Right!

00:09:58.200 --> 00:09:59.060
You can do it!

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:01.160
Go for it, Nakano!

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:03.620
I've got this!

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:11.920
Yikes!

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:13.630
Go!

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:19.410
Nakano-san's putting her speed to good use.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:22.030
Asada-senpai!

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:23.700
I know!

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:24.970
I just need a little...

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:29.480
There!

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:33.710
First!

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:40.780
Nice bunt!

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:43.240
So she was listening at the meeting.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:46.680
To trick the enemy,
you must first trick your allies!

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:48.370
All right, I'm going in.

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:50.210
Tsubasa, make it happen!

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:51.740
I'm on it!

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:59.880
<i>She's the one who was on the winning team
at the Senior Little League nationals, huh?</i>

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:12.980
Stop!

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:14.330
Yay!

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:15.940
Nice batting!

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:22.820
<i>Sayaka...</i>

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:25.780
<i>There's no need to get flustered.</i>

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:35.080
<i>She's thrown nothing but fastballs, too.</i>

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:41.630
<i>Got it!</i>

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:46.720
Nakano-san!

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:48.890
Second!

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.480
<b>Seijo</b>

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.480
<b>Satogahama</b>

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.440
All right!

00:11:57.950 --> 00:11:59.270
We did it!

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:04.190
The Satogahama High School girls' baseball 
association just scored their first run!

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:07.990
We might... actually win?

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:09.680
Let's go for it!

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:11.300
Yeah!

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:27.020
<i>Their right fielder has a first base glove?</i>

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:29.590
<i>But why?</i>

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:32.350
Let's keep this going!

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:34.480
Hi-yah!

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:36.630
Strike three!

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:37.720
Eh?

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:54.830
Strike three!

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:58.740
<i>There's only one reason I can think of.</i>

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.710
<i>Getting a run on the board
in the first inning was ideal.</i>

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:15.020
<i>I have to keep up the momentum.</i>

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:27.530
Strike two!

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:29.740
<i>That was...</i>

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:31.250
What was <i>that</i>?

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:34.700
A slider. It's amazing how
much break she got on that.

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:37.450
Is it even possible to hit that?

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:41.060
So I was right...

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:51.050
I blew it...

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:52.970
Don't worry about it, Tomocchi!

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:54.370
Okay.

00:13:58.840 --> 00:14:00.180
This is our chance.

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:07.740
Ukita-san! Come short!

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.220
S-Sorry...

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:18.900
They haven't scored yet!

00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:27.330
Makino-san, make sure you get on base.

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:28.260
Right.

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:43.820
Ball four!

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:47.300
<i>The bases are loaded...</i>

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:51.540
We're still in this! Stay focused!

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.750
<b>Seijo</b>

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.750
<b>Satogahama</b>

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:02.290
We're still tied!

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:04.250
That's right! There's still time!

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:11.590
Two outs! Two outs!

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.550
<i>The momentum's shifting the other way...</i>

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:16.300
<i>I have to stop them now!</i>

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:19.430
<i>Crap!</i>

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:34.240
They took the lead... that easily?

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:36.280
It's no use.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:40.900
I've figured out her pitches.

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:53.660
<b>Seijo</b>

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:53.660
<b>Satogahama</b>

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:56.050
It's only the third inning!
We still have a chance!

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:57.430
It won't be that easy.

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:01.080
If we come up with a way 
to counter her slider...

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:05.400
It's not just that.
Haven't you noticed it yet?

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:09.730
Seijo's infielders are using 
outfielders' gloves, and vice versa.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.570
The infielders and
outfielders swapped around?

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:20.970
From here on out, they'll be 
playing their real positions.

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:22.790
They tricked us?!

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:27.230
Even if they did,
there's nothing wrong in that.

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:29.500
This is a practice game, after all.

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:34.470
Playing positions they're not used to,
and sacrificing their order's first at-bats

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:37.510
to figure out a pitcher's pitches...

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:42.700
Seijo has been focusing on
their own goals this whole time.

00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:46.710
Their mindset toward this game
is totally different than ours.

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:52.400
We'd lost before this game even started.

00:16:57.140 --> 00:16:59.080
<b>Seijo</b>

00:16:57.140 --> 00:16:59.080
<b>Satogahama</b>

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:00.080
<b>Seijo</b>

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:00.240
<b>Satogahama</b>

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:11.080
Oh, you're the only one here, Tomocchi?

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:12.420
Where's Ukita-san?

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:13.650
She said she'd be late.

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:15.780
What about Suzuki-san and the rest?

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:17.140
They said they'd be late.

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:23.810
Ukita-san?

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:27.510
Shinonome-san...

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:29.390
You're not going to practice?

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:32.090
Because of yesterday?

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:34.780
Um... well...

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:38.020
I get that you feel bad
about the mistakes you made.

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:39.780
I do, too.

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.850
No one's coming.

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:46.180
They're just running a little late.

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:49.590
Maybe it's my fault...

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:50.840
No, it's not!

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:54.350
This was their first game,

00:17:54.350 --> 00:17:58.390
but I guess I got more excited
about it than they did.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:02.070
One!

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:03.770
Two!

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:05.350
Three!

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:06.510
Four!

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:10.840
So... you know... I mean, you...

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:14.030
You weren't the reason we lost.

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:17.950
Thanks.

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:19.540
Forty-six!

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.290
Forty-seven!

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:23.490
Forty-eight!

00:18:24.760 --> 00:18:25.950
Forty-nine!

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:29.920
We're out of balls...

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:32.230
Time to pick them up...

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:33.640
Yeah.

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:50.690
Sorry we're late!

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:54.980
You guys...

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:05.660
Hey, why don't we review the game?

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:06.580
Huh?

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.490
We didn't get to yesterday,
because everyone went straight home.

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:14.070
We should all discuss what we need
to improve. It'll help us in the future.

00:19:17.650 --> 00:19:20.050
Let's start with me.

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:23.980
I got so caught up in winning and losing,

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:30.040
I forgot to set goals we could work on
during the game to help us improve!

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:32.690
I had so much fun practicing,

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:35.980
I failed to scout the other team!

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:39.670
I could've helped Suzuki out!

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:44.200
I let myself get discouraged!

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:47.540
Me, too!

00:19:48.630 --> 00:19:50.170
I got scared.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.560
And you, Shinonome-san?

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:53.630
Huh?

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:58.610
I guess... I lost control of my pitches.

00:19:58.610 --> 00:20:01.550
I didn't cheer us on enough!

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:04.510
Senpai, you need to work on
knowing when to swing!

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:07.010
You're right.

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:07.830
You, Aoi?

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:08.720
Nothing!

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:10.180
Nothing at all?

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:11.670
No, but...

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:13.890
I'm just really frustrated!

00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:17.670
That was the first time
I'd ever lost in a competition!

00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:20.340
Well, I'm frustrated, too.

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:22.400
It goes without saying that I am, too.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.410
We all are.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:26.870
Yeah... Frustrated.

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:33.460
I regret that I committed an error.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:35.930
I think we all did that.

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:37.590
Definitely.

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:42.540
And you, Tsubasa?

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:44.880
I...

00:20:49.150 --> 00:20:51.850
I'm sorry!

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:56.370
I thought none of you were
going to show up today!

00:20:57.170 --> 00:20:58.180
Why?

00:20:58.630 --> 00:20:59.650
Well...

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:02.660
Because we lost so badly?

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:10.030
I got you guys all hyped up
without thinking it through...

00:21:10.030 --> 00:21:13.960
We all said we wanted 
to play a game, too.

00:21:14.530 --> 00:21:17.460
Tsubasa, you put too much
on your own shoulders!

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:23.260
Have more faith in your teammates!

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.230
Uh-huh!

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:37.150
Okay!

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:40.650
That was all rather embarrassing...

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:43.600
Yeah, I guess it was.

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:45.960
We might as well form a huddle or something!

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:48.070
That'd be super embarrassing...

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:49.490
We have to do that?

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:50.520
No way.

00:21:50.520 --> 00:21:51.490
What do you think?

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:53.560
I want to do it!

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:55.000
Well, shall we, then?

00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:56.460
You must be kidding!

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:58.620
What do we do now?

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:00.500
A cheer... I guess?

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:01.560
Okay, then!

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:03.370
Satogahama!

00:22:03.370 --> 00:22:04.960
You're leading the cheer, Senpai?

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:06.190
Don't worry about it.

00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:06.920
Fight!

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:09.720
Yeah!

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:14.930
It's still <i>so</i> frustrating, though!

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:19.940
<b>Next Time</b>

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:19.940
<b>What We Do From Now On</b>
